Effects of organo-floc as natural coagulant on posttreatment of ultrafiltration
membrane
ABSTRACT
Membrane cleaning is necessary in order to restore the performance of the membrane.
However, the cleaning water after membrane cleaning has become the secondary waste
effluent which contains particulates resulting from membrane fouling, membrane
pretreatment and feed concentration. In this work, coagulation method was selected as a posttreatment of UF membrane after treating palm oil mill effluent (POME). The application of
organo-floc (natural coagulant) as a primary coagulant were studied and compared with
aluminum sulphate. The performances of the post-treatment were investigated by the effects
of chemical oxygen demand (COD), total suspended solid (TSS) and color removal. The
optimization of coagulant process using organo-floc was conducted using central composite
design (CCD) in the response surface methodology (RSM).
Keyword: Membrane cleaning; Post-treatment; Coagulation; Palm oil mill effluent;
Response surface methodology


